<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex reports average May crude exports.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex reports average May crude exports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said on Friday it exported an average 1.665 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude oil in May.</p>
<p>Exports for the month fell from an average 1.817 million bpd exported in April, but rose from May 1996, when exports were an average 1.536 million bpd.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of crudes by type and destination:</p>
<p>  Maya exports			     964,700 bpd</p>
<p>  Isthmus exports			  175,000 bpd</p>
<p>  Olmeca exports			   524,800 bpd</p>
<p>Geographical Distribution</p>
<p>    United States				 80 pct</p>
<p>    Spain					    8 pct</p>
<p>    Other America				  5 pct</p>
<p>    Japan					    3 pct</p>
<p>    Other Europe				   2 pct</p>
<p>    Africa					   2 pct</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903)) E-mail at timna.tanners@reuters.com</p>
